From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:46:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: move a code-free i386 image that has no relocation
 directory

An i386 image placed away from its preferred base in the WoW64 window was
refused (STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES) when it had no relocation
directory. Wine's export-only i386 modules have none: usp10.dll is all
forwarders to gdi32, 0x2000 bytes at 0x10000000 with only an export
table. A game DLL at 0x10000000 (Counter-Strike's Mss32.dll) then made
usp10 fail to load, and with it libcef.dll and the game's chromehtml.dll;
the game called a null function and ended (c0000005).

Wine moves such an image with nothing to fix. Do the same for an image the
server found holds no code (contains_code clear); an image with code and no
relocation directory is still refused.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-11-opengl-goldsrc.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c     | 2 +-
 build/ntdll-unix/wow64_placement.h | 9 ++++++---
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
index 7307d16..9acb8e6 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c
@@ -14124,7 +14124,7 @@ static NTSTATUS map_image_into_view( struct file_view *view, const UNICODE_STRIN
     {
         status = ios_wow64_relocate_image( ptr, total_size,
                  get_data_dir( nt, total_size, IMAGE_DIRECTORY_ENTRY_BASERELOC ),
-                 image_info->base, image_info->map_addr );
+                 image_info->base, image_info->map_addr, image_info->contains_code );
         if (status) goto done;
         ((IMAGE_NT_HEADERS32 *)nt)->OptionalHeader.ImageBase = image_info->map_addr;
         dprintf(2, "[wow64-placement] preferred=%#llx guest=%#llx delta=%#x host=%p fixups=guest native_exec=0\n",
diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_placement.h b/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_placement.h
index 8853ae7..ad154e8 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_placement.h
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/wow64_placement.h
@@ -69,13 +69,16 @@ static NTSTATUS ios_wow64_place_image( uintptr_t window, struct pe_image_info *i
 
 /* Validate the whole i386 directory before Wine mutates any target. Storage
  * uses host addresses, but HIGH/LOW/HIGHLOW receive ONLY the guest delta.
- * Unknown types, missing fixups and malformed blocks fail closed. */
+ * Unknown types, missing fixups and malformed blocks fail closed. An image
+ * with no relocation directory moves only when it holds no code (the
+ * server's contains_code): Wine's export-only i386 modules (usp10.dll, all
+ * forwarders) have nothing to fix, and Wine moves them as it does here. */
 static NTSTATUS ios_wow64_relocate_image( char *ptr, size_t size, IMAGE_DATA_DIRECTORY *dir,
-                                         uint32_t preferred, uint32_t guest )
+                                         uint32_t preferred, uint32_t guest, int contains_code )
 {
     size_t offset, end;
     if (guest == preferred) return STATUS_SUCCESS;
-    if (!dir || !dir->Size) return STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES;
+    if (!dir || !dir->Size) return contains_code ? STATUS_CONFLICTING_ADDRESSES : STATUS_SUCCESS;
     if (dir->VirtualAddress >= size || dir->Size > size - dir->VirtualAddress)
         return STATUS_INVALID_IMAGE_FORMAT;
     offset = dir->VirtualAddress;
